---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SleepFlip from "../components/SleepFlip.astro";
import Converter from "../components/Converter.astro";
import { GITHUB_URL, FLASHER_URL, CROSSPOINT_URL } from "../site";

const classics = [
  { title: "Frankenstein", author: "Mary Shelley", pockets: 48, file: "frankenstein-pocket-pages.epub", size: "0.7 MB" },
  { title: "Pride and Prejudice", author: "Jane Austen", pockets: 79, file: "pride-and-prejudice-pocket-pages.epub", size: "0.9 MB" },
  { title: "Moby Dick", author: "Herman Melville", pockets: 149, file: "moby-dick-pocket-pages.epub", size: "1.5 MB" },
];
---
<Base current="home">
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <h1>A whole book, six minutes at a time.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Pocket Pages cuts an EPUB into short reading sessions that stop at natural breaks.
        It's made for the Xteink X4 running CrossPoint: when you finish a session, the reader
        sleeps on a card that shows what comes next.
      </p>
      <p class="lead soft">Six minutes a day adds up to five or six novels a year.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button" href="#convert">Convert a book</a>
        <a class="button quiet" href="#classics">Get a free classic</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-device">
      <SleepFlip />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="convert" class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Convert a book</h2>
      <p class="prose intro">
        Choose any DRM-free EPUB. You get back one file: the same book, arranged into pockets,
        ready to copy to your reader.
      </p>
      <Converter />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="session-h">
    <h2 id="session-h">How a session goes</h2>
    <ol class="session">
      <li>
        <img src="/img/device-opener.webp" width="617" height="960" loading="lazy"
          alt="The reader showing the start of a pocket: Pocket 2 of 61, 6 min read, Book 1, Chapter III, then the first lines of the chapter." />
        <h3>Start</h3>
        <p>Each pocket opens with a small card: which pocket, how long it takes, and where you are in the book. The page count at the bottom counts through this pocket only.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <img src="/img/device-endcard.webp" width="645" height="960" loading="lazy"
          alt="The end card: Pocket 1 complete, 1% read. Up next: Pocket 2, 6 min read, followed by the next pocket's first line in quotes." />
        <h3>Finish</h3>
        <p>About a dozen pages later the pocket ends at a chapter end or a scene break, never mid-paragraph. Turn one more page for the end card.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <img src="/img/device-sleep.webp" width="618" height="960" loading="lazy"
          alt="The same end card as a sleep screen, white text on a dark screen, with a small moon icon in the corner." />
        <h3>Sleep</h3>
        <p>Put the reader down. The end card stays as your sleep screen, so tomorrow's session is waiting the next time you pick it up.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section id="classics" class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Start with a classic</h2>
      <p class="prose intro">
        Ready-made Pocket Pages editions of three novels, from the carefully produced, public-domain
        books at <a href="https://standardebooks.org">Standard Ebooks</a>.
      </p>
      <ul class="shelf">
        {classics.map((b) => (
          <li>
            <div>
              <h3>{b.title}</h3>
              <p class="soft">{b.author}. {b.pockets} pockets, about {Math.ceil(b.pockets / 7)} weeks at one a day.</p>
            </div>
            <a class="button quiet" href={`/books/${b.file}`} download aria-label={`Download ${b.title}, ${b.size}`}>Download ({b.size})</a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="set-up" class="wrap section">
    <h2>Set up your reader</h2>
    <ol class="steps prose">
      <li>
        <h3>Install CrossPoint</h3>
        <p>
          Pocket Pages is built for <a href={CROSSPOINT_URL}>CrossPoint</a>, the free, open-source
          firmware for the Xteink X4 and X4 Pro. Install it with
          the <a href={FLASHER_URL}>CrossPoint web flasher</a>.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Turn on Quick Resume</h3>
        <p>
          On the reader, go to Settings, then Display, and set Sleep Screen to Quick Resume.
          The reader then sleeps on the page you're reading, so finishing on an end card puts
          the next pocket on your sleep screen.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Copy the book across</h3>
        <p>Put the .epub on the reader's SD card and open it from the library. The table of contents lists every pocket with its length.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Optional: the dark sleep screen</h3>
        <p>
          Standard CrossPoint shows the end card as it is, with every line in bold. For the flip to
          white on black, and lighter lines under each heading, I wrote two small changes to CrossPoint:
          a Quick Resume (Dark) sleep screen, and headings that keep regular weight when a book asks for it.
          Until they're in an official CrossPoint release, the changes and an experimental build for the X4 Pro
          are <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/tree/main/firmware`}>on GitHub</a>. If you try the build, you can
          always go back to standard CrossPoint with the web flasher.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap teaser">
      <hr class="card-rule" />
      <h2>Why six minutes?</h2>
      <p class="prose">
        Because it's short enough to do on a bad day and long enough to get somewhere. The maths
        does the rest. The story covers the research behind it, what I heard from e-ink readers,
        and how the end card went from a biro sketch to a sleep screen.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/story">Read the story</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    display: grid; gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem); align-items: center;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.25fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    padding-top: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.5rem);
  }
  .hero-text { max-width: 36rem; }
  .hero h1 { margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
  .lead { font-size: var(--step-1); line-height: 1.5; }
  .lead.soft { font-size: var(--step-0); }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.8rem; margin-top: 1.8rem; }
  .hero-device { --device-w: clamp(220px, 26vw, 300px); justify-self: center; }

  .band { background: var(--panel); padding: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem) 0; }
  .section { padding-top: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem); padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem); }
  h2 { margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
  .intro { margin-bottom: 1.8rem; }

  .session {
    list-style: none; counter-reset: s; margin: 2rem 0 0; padding: 0;
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: clamp(1.2rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
  }
  .session li { counter-increment: s; }
  .session img { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 5 / 7.6; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 8px; background: var(--panel); }
  .session h3 { margin: 1rem 0 0.4rem; display: flex; gap: 0.55rem; align-items: baseline; }
  .session h3::before { content: counter(s); font-weight: 400; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .session p { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }

  .shelf { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; max-width: 46rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .shelf li {
    display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 1rem 2rem; flex-wrap: wrap;
    padding: 1.15rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .shelf h3 { margin-bottom: 0.15rem; }
  .shelf p { margin: 0; font-size: 1rem; }

  .steps { list-style: none; counter-reset: st; padding: 0; margin: 2rem 0 0; display: grid; gap: 1.8rem; }
  .steps li { counter-increment: st; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2.2rem minmax(0, 1fr); column-gap: 0.4rem; }
  .steps li::before { content: counter(st); grid-row: 1 / span 2; font-size: var(--step-1); line-height: 1.3; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .steps h3 { margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }

  .teaser { display: grid; gap: 1rem; justify-items: start; }
  .teaser h2 { margin: 0.6rem 0 0; }
  .teaser p { margin: 0; }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .hero-device { --device-w: min(62vw, 250px); }
    .session { grid-template-columns: 1fr; max-width: 24rem; }
  }
</style>
